abstract: >-
  A small-scale comparison of pre-consent third-party tracking on
  domestic violence support websites in the United Kingdom and the
  United States. Methodology: ~50 UK and ~50 US sites; aggregate
  descriptive comparison by jurisdiction; repeated per-site visits under
  OpenWPM-instrumented, pinned, unbranded Firefox; a residential-exit
  HTTP relay; tracker classification against pinned snapshots of
  DuckDuckGo Tracker Radar and EasyPrivacy.
